checkModuleDeclarations is operation
checkModuleDeclarations purpose "Check the entities of one module of a program and collect its declarations, under its own names, in maps seeded with the built-in names and every earlier module's `<module>.<name>`; then publish its names as `<module>.<name>` for the modules after it"
checkModuleDeclarations invariant declaresTypes "\"Built-in types are numbered 1 to 11 (String, Int64, ExitCode, Bool, Byte, Region, the standard errors, ByteBuffer, process.Arguments, time.Deadline, Bytes) and every record, enum, typeInstance, table, and operationType of the program after them in source order; each record field and enum variant is a member, in order\""
checkModuleDeclarations invariant declaresTargets "\"Every standard library target of the subset, operation, record constructor and field reader, enum variant constructor, list and map member, and table reader is a call target with its slots, result type, and error, under its own name in its module and as `<module>.<name>` in the modules after it\""
checkModuleDeclarations invariant rejectsOutsideDeclarations "\"A predicate, payload, type, or kind outside the subset is refused at the word concerned, as is a module whose first entity is not its module entity, a main that takes inputs, a type held by value before it is declared, and a call or region whose operation does not exist\""
